rep('''    t1 = table(["Row", "Core", "CME", "Source", "Note"],''', '''    cme_add = ''', '''    t1 = table(["Row", "Core", "CME", "Source", "Note"],
               [["Dependent load, 4 KiB chain", f"{c[(4096, 'repeat')]['core']:.1f} ns", f"{c[(4096, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"round-trip baseline (DUP, LASTB, no load) {rt:.1f} ns = {rt_cyc:.0f} CME cycles, chain load minus round-trip baseline {c[(4096, 'repeat')]['ns'] - rt:.2f} ns (derived). Run 3 {c[(4096, 'repeat')]['ns3']:.1f} ns, boot F1 {CLV1[(4096, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f}"],
                ["L1 hit, dependent load, 4 to 64 KiB, CME prefetcher off", f"{c[(4096, 'repeat')]['core']:.1f} ns (4 KiB)", f"{min(b_l1):.1f} to {max(b_l1):.1f} ns", "boots B, F2", f"every load hits the CME L1: boot B (L3 off) {min(b_l1):.2f} to {max(b_l1):.2f} ns, boot F2 (L3 on) {CLV2[(4096, 'repeat')]['ns']:.2f} to {CLV2[(65536, 'repeat')]['ns']:.2f}. Minus the {rt_b:.1f} ns round-trip baseline: {min(b_l1) - rt_b:.2f} to {max(b_l1) - rt_b:.2f} ns (derived). Boot E's times: next row"],
                ["8 KiB / 16 KiB / 64 KiB", f"{k8['core']:.1f} / {k16['core']:.1f} / {c[(65536, 'repeat')]['core']:.1f} ns", f"{k8['ns']:.1f} / {k16['ns']:.1f} / {c[(65536, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"run 3: {k8['ns3']:.1f} / {k16['ns3']:.1f} / {c[(65536, 'repeat')]['ns3']:.1f} ns; boot F1 (run 6): {CLV1[(8192, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f} / {CLV1[(16384, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f} / {CLV1[(65536, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f}. The climb is the CME prefetcher's: with it off (boots B, F2) {cb[8192]:.1f} / {cb[16384]:.1f} / {cb[65536]:.1f} ns"],
                ["L3-served load, 192 / 256 / 384 KiB chain, CME prefetcher off", f"{HIT[196608]['ns']:.1f} / {HIT[262144]['ns']:.1f} / {HIT[393216]['ns']:.1f} ns (boot E)", " / ".join(f"{f2_l3[s]['ns']:.1f}" for s in L3S) + " ns", "boot F2 (run 6)", f"one demand refill per load, all from inside the cluster ({f2_in[0]:.2f} to {f2_in[1]:.2f} inner, {f2_out[0]:.2f} to {f2_out[1]:.2f} outer per load). Minus the baseline: " + " / ".join(f"{f2_l3[s]['ns'] - rt6:.1f}" for s in L3S) + f" ns (derived). The exploratory L3-hit event puts {CL3_2[(196608, 'repeat')]['hit']:.2f} to {CL3_2[(393216, 'repeat')]['hit']:.2f} of the loads in the L3 and the rest in CPU 2's own cache (hypothesis). Boot B, the L3 off: " + " / ".join(f"{cb[s]:.1f}" for s in L3S) + "; the prefetcher on (F1): " + " / ".join(f"{CLV1[(s, 'repeat')]['ns']:.1f}" for s in L3S)],
                ["2 MiB chain walked once (SLC on the core)", f"{c[(2097152, 'fresh')]['core']:.1f} ns", f"{c[(2097152, 'fresh')]['ns']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"run 3 {c[(2097152, 'fresh')]['ns3']:.1f} ns; boot F1 {CLV1[(2097152, 'fresh')]['ns']:.1f}, boot F2 (prefetchers off) {CLV2[(2097152, 'fresh')]['ns']:.1f}"],
                ["DRAM (emulator memory model, fixed delay), 8 MiB random chain, every line flushed from all caches", f"{c[(8388608, 'flushed')]['core']:.1f} ns", f"{c[(8388608, 'flushed')]['ns']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"run 3 {c[(8388608, 'flushed')]['ns3']:.1f} ns, boot C {c[(8388608, 'flushed')]['nsC']:.1f}, boot F1 {CLV1[(8388608, 'flushed')]['ns']:.1f}; prefetchers off: boot F2 {CLV2[(8388608, 'flushed')]['ns']:.1f}, boot B {p.CME_FLUSHED['B']:.1f} (the prefetcher, not the L3, sets this row)"],
                ["DRAM (emulator memory model, fixed delay), 8 MiB chain in address order, every line flushed first", f"{c[(8388608, 'seq')]['core']:.1f} ns", f"{c[(8388608, 'seq')]['ns']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"every CME refill a prefetch ({c[(8388608, 'seq')]['e']['cme_l1d_refill_hwprf']:.2f} per load). The same {p.CME_SEQ['A']:.1f} ns on boots A and C, {p.CME_SEQ['B']:.1f} ns with the prefetcher off (boot B). The memory model has no configured delay (Jesse's F1 README: every delay control zero, a 3 ns native response; the rest is RTL pipeline, an inference)"],
                ["OCM, one region, 1 to 3 crosspoints", f"{min(core_sp):.1f} to {max(core_sp):.1f} ns", f"{min(f2_sp):.1f} to {max(f2_sp):.1f} ns (F2, demand only); {min(e_sp):.1f} to {max(e_sp):.1f} (E)", "boots F2, E", f"chain with one line per 4 KiB page, best of 7 passes of 64 loads. With the prefetchers off (F2) every load's line comes from outside the cluster: the demand-only OCM latency through the CME. With the prefetcher on (E, F1 {min(f1_sp):.1f} to {max(f1_sp):.1f}, run 3 {min(r3_sp):.1f} to {max(r3_sp):.1f}) it fetches part of each line first. The core's values here are below the true OCM latency: on boot E only {p.SPARSE_L3_RNG_CPU2['E'][0]:.2f} to {p.SPARSE_L3_RNG_CPU2['E'][1]:.2f} of its loads are read from the mesh"],
                ["OCM, all five regions, chain over every line", f"{p.ALL5[2]['E']['dense']:.1f} ns", f"{p.CME_ALL5['E']['dense']:.1f} ns", "boot E", f"20,480 loads a pass. Run 3 CME {p.CME_ALL5['run3']['dense']:.1f} ns, boot F1 {C1['CALL5D']['best']:.1f}, boot F2 {C2['CALL5D']['best']:.1f}"],
                ["L1 read / write bandwidth, single-call form, 4 to 48 KiB", f"{g8[('asm', 'read', 24576)]['agg']['E']:.1f} / {g8[('asm', 'write', 24576)]['agg']['E']:.1f} GB/s at 24 KiB (boot E)", f"{min(SINGLE_RD):.0f} to {max(SINGLE_RD):.0f} / {min(SINGLE_WR):.0f} to {max(SINGLE_WR):.0f} GB/s", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"{BPC6 * min(SINGLE_RD):.0f} to {BPC6 * max(SINGLE_RD):.0f} / {BPC6 * min(SINGLE_WR):.0f} bytes per CME cycle: one 64-byte load per cycle and {BPC6 * max(SINGLE_WR) / 64:.2f} of a store, measured with every pass of a rep inside one call. The looped form (one call per pass) reads {FORM1[('looped', 'read')]['rows'][24576]['agg']:.0f} / {FORM1[('looped', 'write')]['rows'][24576]['agg']:.0f} GB/s at 24 KiB: the call's cost hides the rate"],
                ["CME pipeline widths (hardware)", "", "2 loads or stores per cycle", "Arm guides", f"the core issues up to 3 SME instructions per cycle, loads and stores 2 [C1-Nano SOG 109590, section 2.33]. CME L1: 4-way, 16 banks, two 512-bit read paths [C1-SME2 TRM 107831, table 6-1]. The public LLVM model (the compiler's timing table for this core) gives a contiguous streaming load or store 1 per cycle, 2 CME cycles of latency [refs/C1Nano-streaming-cme-instructions.s]. Measured (F1): one load and {BPC6 * max(SINGLE_WR) / 64:.1f} of a store per cycle with the L3 on (run 3, the L3 off: half a store). Why stores stop there is Insufficient data (no store path width in the sources on disk)"],
                ["Read bandwidth, 48 KiB buffer", f"{ONE1[49152]['read']:.1f} GB/s", f"{CBW1[49152]['read']['agg']:.1f} GB/s ({CBW1[49152]['read']['span']:.1f} in span)", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"the CME's peak. In span is the rate inside the streaming span; the bracket adds each call's save, SMSTART, SMSTOP, restore and run 6's two in-span clock reads. Run 3, the L3 off: {b48['read']:.1f} by the bracket (core {b48['core_read']:.1f})"],
                ["Read bandwidth, 160 KiB to 32 MiB", f"{ONE1[33554432]['read']:.1f} GB/s at 32 MiB", f"{min(d['read']['agg'] for d in big1):.1f} to {max(d['read']['agg'] for d in big1):.1f} GB/s", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"{CBW1[33554432]['read']['agg'] / ONE1[33554432]['read']:.1f} times the core at 32 MiB (run 3, the L3 off: {b32m['read']:.1f} against the core's {b32m['core_read']:.1f}). With the CME prefetcher off (F2) {CBW2[33554432]['read']['agg']:.1f} GB/s at 32 MiB: the prefetcher carries half of a DRAM stream"],
                ["Write bandwidth, 16 KiB to 32 MiB", f"{min(ONE1[s]['write'] for s in ONE1):.1f} to {max(ONE1[s]['write'] for s in ONE1):.1f} GB/s", f"{min(d['write']['agg'] for d in C1['CBW']):.1f} to {max(d['write']['agg'] for d in C1['CBW']):.1f} GB/s", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"{CBW1[262144]['write']['agg']:.0f} GB/s to 256 KiB and {CBW1[33554432]['write']['agg']:.0f} from 1 MiB, in span too, on F1 and F2 alike; run 3 wrote {min(d['write'] for d in CBW):.0f} to {max(d['write'] for d in CBW):.0f} at every footprint with the L3 off, so the L3 on costs the CME's writes. Why is open (full page, section 10)"],
                ["OCM read / streaming write, all five", f"{OCMBW1['all5']:.1f} / {OCMBW1['write']:.1f} GB/s", f"{COCMBW1['all5']:.1f} / {COCMBW1['write']:.1f} GB/s", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"run 3, the L3 off: {COCMBW['all5']:.1f} / {COCMBW['write']:.1f} through the CME, {OCMBW['all5']:.1f} / {OCMBW['write']:.1f} from the core"],
                ["Cost per call (the four L1 forms, 4 to 24 KiB)", "", f"read call about {FORM1[('looped', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns'] - FORM1[('single', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns']:.0f} ns, {FORM1[('looped', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns'] - FORM1[('nofold', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns']:.0f} of it the fold", "boot F1 (run 6)", f"the looped read's line (ns per pass against bytes) gives {FORM1[('looped', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns']:.0f} ns per pass, the single-call read's {FORM1[('single', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns']:.1f}, the read without its fold {FORM1[('nofold', 'read')]['fit']['a_ns']:.0f}. A write call hides its cost behind its posted stores (the looped write's points are not a line); DSB ST before SMSTOP adds {FORM1[('dsb', 'write')]['rows'][4096]['t_pass'] - FORM1[('looped', 'write')]['rows'][4096]['t_pass']:.0f} to {FORM1[('dsb', 'write')]['rows'][8192]['t_pass'] - FORM1[('looped', 'write')]['rows'][8192]['t_pass']:.0f} ns per pass. Run 6's in-span clock reads add about {C1['CALL_NS'][0] - g.CALL_NS[0]:.0f} ns to a one-instruction call (cme-call {C1['CALL_NS'][0]:.0f} ns against run 3's {g.CALL_NS[0]:.0f})"]],
               "CPU 2 with CPU 3 offline, so the DSU's CME serves one core. Best rep or best pass of each row [cme-latency-*.csv of boots E, B, F1 and F2, cme-bandwidth-*.csv of boot F1 (run 6) and run 3, and the same runs' core rows]. GB = 1e9 bytes. Run 6's --cme rows carry a second time read inside the streaming span (in span) beside the bracket.")
''')
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the body
sub('''<dt>run, boot</dt><dd>A run is one job on the emulator (run 3 = membench-jibin-004). Run 4 is five boots, A to E: A as run 3, B the prefetchers off (the CME's too), C and D the OCM mapped with a 64 KiB hint (D with the prefetchers off), E the L3 on.</dd>
<dt>streaming mode</dt>''', '''<dt>run, boot</dt><dd>A run is one job on the emulator (run 3 = membench-jibin-004). Run 4 is five boots, A to E: A as run 3, B the prefetchers off (the CME's too), C and D the OCM mapped with a 64 KiB hint (D with the prefetchers off), E the L3 on. Run 6 (commit 0c190a1) is two boots on boot E's SCP: F1 the L3 on with the prefetchers on (every CME row and the core rows), F2 the L3 on with the prefetchers of the cores and the CMEs off (the CME rows).</dd>
<dt>bracket, in span</dt><dd>Run 6 times every CME call twice: by the clock reads around the call (bracket) and by clock reads inside the streaming span (in span, after SMSTART and before SMSTOP).</dd>
<dt>looped form, single-call form</dt><dd>An L1 bandwidth row with one call of the kernel per pass (looped), or with every pass of a rep inside one call and one streaming span (single-call).</dd>
<dt>streaming mode</dt>''')
sub('''and steps by {cb[98304] - cb[65536]:+.1f} ns at 96 KiB. The core steps at 48 KiB,''', '''and steps by {cb[98304] - cb[65536]:+.1f} ns at 96 KiB. Boot F2 (run 6: the L3 on, the prefetchers off) repeats boot B to 64 KiB and reads {min(d['ns'] for d in f2_l3.values()):.1f} to {max(d['ns'] for d in f2_l3.values()):.1f} ns at 192 to 384 KiB, where the L3 serves it. The core steps at 48 KiB,''')
